" hestia video-rig .vimrc (light) — NOT anyone's personal vimrc: no plugins,
" no personal keymaps. Staged as $HOME/.vimrc for hestia-video recordings
" (docs/video-capture-design.md) so a clip's editor behaviour is identical
" no matter which real user renders it. `colorscheme hestia` resolves via
" $HOME/.vim/colors/hestia.vim — hestia-video copies that file in fresh
" from the repo each run, not a symlink to anyone's personal ~/.vim.
set nocompatible
set termguicolors
set number
set relativenumber
set cursorline
set laststatus=2
set colorcolumn=80
syntax on
set background=light
colorscheme hestia

" `filetype indent on` (part of the common `filetype plugin indent on`) is
" DELIBERATELY not loaded — its per-language auto-indent-on-Enter/{/}
" DOUBLES literal leading whitespace typed on top of it (confirmed live:
" 4-space C source came out at 6, then 10 spaces per subsequent line — see
" docs/video-capture-design.md §11). `filetype plugin on` alone still gives
" filetype detection/syntax/ftplugin settings without that conflict, so a
" scene's typed text is exactly what ends up on screen — no on-camera
" `:setlocal` workaround needed, and no per-scene indent guessing either.
filetype plugin on
set shiftwidth=4 tabstop=4 expandtab

" Minimal auto-pairs, hand-rolled rather than installing a plugin (owner,
" 2026-08-19: their real personal profile uses coc.nvim's coc-pairs, but
" coc.nvim is a full LSP/completion framework — far too heavy for a rig
" that's deliberately plugin-free). Replicates just the BEHAVIOUR: typing
" an opener inserts its closer immediately with the cursor between them;
" typing the closer when it's already the very next character moves over
" it instead of inserting a second one, so existing scenes (which already
" type BOTH characters of a pair explicitly) need no rewriting.
" Deliberately NOT "smart" — no backspace-deletes-empty-pair-together —
" BackSpace always removes exactly one character, which comment: 's
" exact-count cleanup (hestia-video's emit_comment_line) depends on.
"
" /* */ comments are NOT handled here, deliberately: `a / *ptr` (division
" then a pointer dereference) also contains the sequence "/","*" — a
" naive auto-pair rule on that trigger risks a phantom */ in real code
" that isn't a comment. hestia-video's comment: action handles /* */
" immediate-closing itself (see emit_comment_line), where the tool KNOWS
" it's typing a comment rather than guessing from two characters.
function! s:PairOpen(open, close)
  return a:open . a:close . "\<Left>"
endfunction
function! s:PairSkip(char)
  if getline('.')[col('.') - 1] ==# a:char
    return "\<Right>"
  endif
  return a:char
endfunction
function! s:QuotePair(q)
  if getline('.')[col('.') - 1] ==# a:q
    return "\<Right>"
  endif
  return a:q . a:q . "\<Left>"
endfunction
inoremap <expr> ( <SID>PairOpen('(', ')')
inoremap <expr> [ <SID>PairOpen('[', ']')
inoremap <expr> { <SID>PairOpen('{', '}')
inoremap <expr> ) <SID>PairSkip(')')
inoremap <expr> ] <SID>PairSkip(']')
inoremap <expr> } <SID>PairSkip('}')
inoremap <expr> " <SID>QuotePair('"')
inoremap <expr> ' <SID>QuotePair("'")

autocmd VimEnter * redraw | echo ''
